    <processInformation>
        <dataSetInformation>
            <common:UUID>6f4dc549-972a-32a8-b565-8b0eea0bbeee</common:UUID>
            <name>
                <baseName xml:lang="en">Plugs, inlet and outlet, for printer cable, at plant</baseName>
            </name>
            <classificationInformation>
                <common:classification>
                    <common:class level="0" classId="57aded3d-4d3f-3d65-b03a-7392ab36aef2">electronics</common:class>
                    <common:class level="1" classId="296c829f-9160-371d-9441-529c080d79d5">devices</common:class>
                </common:classification>
            </classificationInformation>
            <common:generalComment xml:lang="en">This dataset can be applied to describe the production of a typical set of plugs (inlet and outlet) for a printer cable. The total weight of the inlet plug (with pins) is 0.0395 kg and 0.050 kg for the outlet plug (the one with holes). The information for this dataset is based on weighing, measurements and analysis at EMPA Laboratories. Updates were made in 2023 to reflect regionalized material and electricity mix for global production; UUID: 6f4dc549-972a-32a8-b565-8b0eea0bbeee</common:generalComment>
        </dataSetInformation>
        <quantitativeReference type="Reference flow(s)">
            <referenceToReferenceFlow>1</referenceToReferenceFlow>
        </quantitativeReference>
        <time xmlns:olca="http://openlca.org/ilcd-extensions" olca:startDate="1672527600000" olca:endDate="1890774000000">
            <common:referenceYear>2023</common:referenceYear>
            <common:dataSetValidUntil>2029</common:dataSetValidUntil>
            <common:timeRepresentativenessDescription xml:lang="en">Unspecified</common:timeRepresentativenessDescription>
        </time>
        <geography>
            <locationOfOperationSupplyOrProduction location="GLO">
                <descriptionOfRestrictions xml:lang="en">The data describes a typical set of plugs for a printer cable in 2006. Plugs and cable are produced by international manufacturers and available all over the world. Therefore a global dataset is justifiable.</descriptionOfRestrictions>
            </locationOfOperationSupplyOrProduction>
        </geography>
        <technology>
            <technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses xml:lang="en">The manufacturing process is inventoried through wire drawing, injection moulding, sheet rolling &amp; hot rolling (steel), contouring (brass), and zinc coating (galvanising of steel).\n\n# Included processes\nDescribes the production of a typical set of inlet and outlet plugs for a printer cable. Calculated per 1 unit of plugs, which is per definition 1 inlet and 1 outlet plug. Included are the materials PVC, LDPE, HDPE, silicone, low-alloyed steel, chromium steel, brass, and copper with their respective manufacturing processes. The infrastructure is calculated via the proxy "electronic component production plant". Further inventoried are the electricity used in the assembly of the plugs, plus the road and rail transportation for input materials from the regional storage to the production site.</technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>
        </technology>
    </processInformation>
